// ============================================================================
//  mod_wavegun.zone  -  the BO1 Wave Gun / Zap Guns, complete   (v2.10.14)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Replaces mod_zapgun.zone (v2.9.18-v2.10.13). The user's directive of
//  2026-09-03 delivered the missing half: Zombies Declassified BETA 1 (the
//  PC port of the cancelled BO2 DLC5) ships Moon as a native T6 zone, and that
//  zone carries the ENTIRE Wave Gun package in T6 form - the combined gun
//  included. Nothing here is a lookalike any more: models, animations,
//  effects, materials and sounds are Treyarch's own BO1 assets as converted for
//  DLC5.
//
//  THE DONOR is zone_source\wavegun_donor\mod.ff - 191 assets copied out of the
//  DLC5 zm_moon.ff with the patched OAT in H:\Claude\oat-dlc5 (the stock
//  Linker cannot read that dev zone; recipe beside the donor). It is --load'ed
//  LAST in build_ff.bat, so first-load-wins means it can only supply names no
//  zombies fastfile above offers; the one shared name it carries,
//  mc/mtl_zombie_teleporter_glow (the gun's glowing parts), therefore resolves
//  from its existing owner. A/B the asset list if the load order ever moves.
//
//  WHAT IS DECLARED HERE:
//    - the 6 xmodels (combined / front / rear x view / world) and the two gun
//      materials; their images and the two DLC5 techsets follow as
//      dependencies.
//    - hud_icon_colt: BO1's OWN Zap Gun HUD icon (measured from BO1's
//      zombie_moon.ff defs, 2026-09-03: dw/lh = hud_icon_colt, combined =
//      hud_thundergun, which this mod already owns via ww_donor).
//    - the 49 viewmodel xanims the six defs reference (the 50th,
//      viewmodel_base_viewhands, is stock).
//    - all 28 weapon/microwavegun + fx_microwavegun_* effects. FX are copied
//      between fastfiles by the Linker - only RAW fx are impossible.
//    - camo,camo_microwavegun: OUR raw zone_assets\camo\camo_microwavegun.json
//      (the DLC5 zone's camo of that name is a hacked camo_sa58 with one slot),
//      built in the shape of camo_zapgun.json with the two raygun_moon
//      materials, so every Pack-a-Punch camo slot works like every other gun.
//      Raw beats every --load for camo (CLAUDE.md precedence table).
//
//  WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT HERE:
//    - weapon defs: raw runtime files in weapons\zm\ (the six DLC5 defs, trimmed
//      under the 20,480 B loader ceiling, hideTags cleared to BO1's own empty
//      value - DLC5's "polysurface73" is a shared-pointer artefact of its
//      writer). Never Linker-copy a DLC5 def: 59 of its 141 weapons share one
//      hideTags array by an absolute pointer the stock loader misresolves.
//    - sounds: 71 rows / 48 aliases in soundbank\mod.all.aliases.additions.csv,
//      payloads under sound\wpn\wavegun\, all dumped from the DLC5 Moon bank
//      (hash-only alias names recovered with OAT's SND_HashName).
//    - the zombie sizzle / zap death anims: present in the DLC5 zone but bound
//      to Moon's aitypes; a stock aitype's compiled anim list cannot take them
//      (ERROR_CATALOGUE §45), so the script's own fallbacks run.
// ============================================================================
xmodel,t5_weapn_raygun_moon_combined_vm
xmodel,t5_weapn_raygun_moon_combined_world
xmodel,t5_weapn_raygun_moon_front_vm
xmodel,t5_weapn_raygun_moon_front_world
xmodel,t5_weapn_raygun_moon_rear_vm
xmodel,t5_weapn_raygun_moon_rear_world
material,mc/mtl_raygun_moon_front
material,mc/mtl_raygun_moon_rear
material,hud_icon_colt
camo,camo_microwavegun

